From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] audio/sdl: open the playback device off the BQL

What: the SDL backend opens and closes the playback device on helper
threads; the BQL never waits for CoreAudio. sdl_init_out() no longer opens
a device at all (it only checked one and closed it again), and a stream
start only starts an open (sdl_enable_out). run_buffer_out takes the device
once it is open. Until then the guest's sound waits in the ring, as it did
behind the blocking open. If SDL has not opened it within 3 s, or the open
failed, the voice drops the sound at the stream's rate (the guest plays to
nobody, the VM runs) and logs once:
  Try Omarchy: sound: the Mac's audio device does not answer (no start within 3 s); the VM goes on without sound
No other playback open starts while one is stuck. A stuck open that returns
with a device is used if the guest still plays ("Try Omarchy: sound: the Mac's
audio device works again"); one that fails after it was stuck is tried
again 5 s later. Closing (stream stop, route switch) happens on a thread
after the callback has stopped.

Why: on the Mac mini (2026-10-05, coreaudiod up for 7 days, a Scarlett 2i2
as the default output) every AudioQueueStart() blocked. SDL3's
COREAUDIO_OpenDevice waits for its device thread, which waited there, so
QEMU hung for good in qemu_init -> hda_audio_init -> sdl_init_out (main
thread, no window, guest never ran, QMP dead). A stream start under the BQL
would hang a running VM the same way.

The time limit starts once the open has sdl_open_lock: a recording open may
hold it for minutes (a pending microphone permission,
qemu-sdl-audio-capture-thread.patch); playback then waits as it did before.

Applies after qemu-sdl-audio-device-selection.patch and
qemu-sdl-audio-capture-thread.patch.

Upstream: the blocking open under the BQL is upstream's too, but this builds
on the try-omarchy route and capture patches; not sent.

Tested in OmacVM: Tests/audio/wedged-output-start.c blocks AudioQueueStart(), injected
into a re-signed copy of the runtime, headless 4-vCPU test VM, a 6 s tone
played twice in the guest with a stream stop between (audio-crackle notes,
"Start hang"). Before: QMP never answered; sample showed the field stack.
After, blocked forever: QMP answers within 2 s, the session is up in 18 s
(as without the library); the first tone takes 9.6 s (3 s wait, then
dropped at its rate), the second 6.6 s; QMP answers during both; the VM
powers off in 3 s with the open still stuck. Device dies after the first
stream (AQHANG_AFTER=1): tone 1 plays, tone 2 as above. Device answers
again (AQHANG_UNTIL): "works again" 5 s later, tone 2 plays. Blocked start
then fails (AQHANG_FAIL, coreaudiod killed): retried 5 s later, "works
again". Without the library: two opens at 44.1 kHz S16 stereo 512 frames as
before, tones take 6.6 s, no warning (sdlprobe). src/tests/audio-timing.sh
(CI) checks the build order, the log lines against omacvm check and that
the stub builds.

Adapted from OmacVM's patch of the same name (MIT,
https://github.com/gillesgoetsch/OmacVM), with its log lines and
environment variable renamed for Try Omarchy.

